      "feedback": "Yes. Content-only, I think this is a **strong raw draft with several excellent facts, but I would tighten it substantially and correct a few claims before publishing.** The biggest issue isn't lack of good material; it's that some themes are repeated three or four times, while a handful of statements are more confident than the evidence warrants. \n\n**The teaser is the first thing I would change.** “Otters are sensitive to water pollution, so a sighting here…means the water is clean enough to hold a healthy food web” overstates what one otter sighting can tell you. Otters travel widely and occur in some fairly human-altered waterways. They can be useful biomonitoring organisms, particularly because contaminants accumulate in them, but *otter present = clean water* is too neat. The ecological-role section repeats essentially the same claim.   I would either soften this considerably or choose a different teaser altogether.\n\nThe **first Quick Hit is terrific material**, especially the whis",
